OL,3,GNEWSAInside the shop that inspired the
OL,4,Asecond-hand fashion boom
OL,5,
OL,6,F"I really love shopping second hand...
OL,7,Fthere's a lot of textiles and a lot of
OL,8,Fwaste already out in the world."
OL,10,FCarolyn Abramowich, 25, is sifting
OL,11,Fthrough the rails of the UK's
OL,12,Ffirst-ever charity shop, Oxfam, which
OL,13,Fopened its doors on Oxford's Broad
OL,14,FStreet back in 1947.
OL,16,F"You're saving things from hitting the
OL,17,Flandfills which is awesome," says
OL,18,FCarolyn, who turned to shopping in
OL,19,Fcharity shops out of concern for the
OL,20,Fenvironment.
OL,23,APub: 05-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
